  (text "NOTES\n1. Cell connects to the module's B+/B- only. The load (amp VBAT/GND) connects to OUT+/OUT- so the protection IC is in the load path.\n2. One speaker on ONE channel (L+/L-). Leave R+/R- open and never tie L- and R- together.\n3. Do not use the amp's micro-USB or its 5V pad while the battery is on VBAT.\n4. DESIGN GAP: no power switch. The amp powers up whenever the cell is connected. A slide switch in series with\n    VOUT_P -> VBAT would add an off state (needs an enclosure cutout).\n5. The TP4056 module does not do true load-sharing: charge with the speaker off to get a proper full-charge indication.\n6. Before connecting the cell, confirm the charge module has THREE chips (TP4056, DW01A, 8205A).\n7. Connect the cell last and check polarity with a meter.\n\nPARTS\nJ1  any 5 V USB-C supply, >= 1 A\nU1  TP4056 Type-C module with DW01A + 8205A protection, ~28 x 17 mm (ShillehTek or equivalent)\nU2  MH-M38 Bluetooth 4.2 amp, 45 x 20 mm (DFRobot DFR0720 is this module)\nBT1 Samsung INR18650-25R, flat top, UNPROTECTED\nLS1 40 mm 4 ohm driver, 20 mm tall or less (Adafruit 3968 or equivalent)" (at 30.48 110.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 8e48619e-6181-4542-8f18-340c8498d659))

